From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:52:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Write the idle slot setup again after a reset

The component probe resets the amp and reinitialises the register
cache, which clears the SDOUT idle slot mask and the force-0 enable.
The idle slot setup cached in the driver data survives the reset,
though, so when the card binds again and set_tdm_idle() asks for the
same mask and mode, it returns early and the force-0 enable is never
written.  set_bclk_ratio() writes the mask again but not the enable.

On the J713 every rebind of the speaker card left the two amps that
force their idle slots to zero without the enable, and the other two
amps' voltage sense words then came back with the top bit set in about
a quarter of the frames.  The speaker protection daemon reads those as a
voltage without current and holds the speakers at a safe level.

Clear the cached setup after the reset, so that the next set_tdm_idle()
writes it.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit c8d20c82d5da78904ed948205978117af34187bb)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 6f4874a80a..0775206da7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -1037,6 +1037,10 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	tas2764_reset(tas2764);
 	regmap_reinit_cache(tas2764->regmap, &tas2764_i2c_regmap);
 
+	/* The reset cleared the idle slot setup: make the next set_tdm_idle() write it */
+	tas2764->idle_slot_config.tx_mask = 0;
+	tas2764->idle_slot_config.tx_mode = SND_SOC_DAI_TDM_IDLE_NONE;
+
 	if (tas2764->irq) {
 		ret = snd_soc_component_write(tas2764->component, TAS2764_INT_MASK0, 0x00);
 		if (ret < 0)
